	(footprint "Connector_JST:JST_XH_B4B-XH-A_1x04_P2.50mm_Vertical"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c6daeb62-320f-31b8-75d9-7c91840868ea")
		(at 95 237)
		(descr "JST B4B-XH-A(LF)(SN) 4-position, 2.50mm pitch, vertical THT wire-to-board header (J_RTD1 pan-probe connector, docs/CONNECTORS_AND_WIRING.md; elec/src/components.ato JST_XH_B4B_XH_A). Hand-built project-local footprint: this environment has no kicad-footprints checkout (Connector_JST.pretty is not available system-wide), so this is not a copy of the official KiCad library footprint. Overall housing envelope (12.4mm x 5.75mm, 7.0mm tall) sourced from JST's published outline for the B*B-XH-A(LF)(SN) THT series (confirmed via DigiKey/Octopart listings for B4B-XH-A, 2026-08-11 -- primary JST PDF was not directly fetchable in this environment, so treat the housing envelope as datasheet-order-of-magnitude, not pin-precise). Pin geometry (2.50mm pitch, 4 in a row, pad 1 keyed) matches the JST XH series spec exactly, which is not part-specific and not in question. Pad size/drill (1.7mm pad / 1.0mm drill) is a standard THT annular ring for this pin gauge, not scaled from a datasheet dimension. LV-signal connector only (RTD sensing, 3A/250V rated per docs/CONNECTORS_AND_WIRING.md) -- not in the HV/mains domain, so this footprint's precision does not affect creepage/clearance measurements against the HV isolation barrier.")
